  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "Many languages need separate verbs for contacting someone by telephone (sense 1) and giving something a name (sense 2); English uses one word for both.",
    "grammar": "The name sense has no word for *as* between object and name: *they called him Lee*, not *called him as Lee*. The phone sense takes a direct object, not a preposition.",
